//! **EF-9.0 -- what "refines sooner" buys. Measurement only; no output change.**
//!
//! `ELEVATION_FIELD_ARCHITECTURE_RESEARCH.md` §8.3, milestone EF-9.0. This file
//! builds no refinement and changes no generated byte. It answers one question
//! with a number: would an importance-driven tile order (river corridors,
//! steep ground, settlements first) capture materially more of what
//! refinement adds than today's centre-distance order -- the gate that decides
//! whether EF-9.1 onward is worth building at all.
//!
//! ```text
//! cargo test --release -p cartalith-civ --test ef9_refinement_gain -- --ignored --nocapture
//! EF9_SEEDS=483920 EF9_GRIDS=512x384 EF9_WINDOW=8 EF9_K=2 ...   # a cheaper run
//! ```
//!
//! # Why a test file and not the doc's `examples/ef9_refinement_gain.rs`
//!
//! The plan names an example. `cargo test` does not run `#[test]`s inside an
//! example, and EF-9.0 needs a committed regression test of the pure scoring
//! functions beside the (ignored) measurement. An integration test holds both,
//! in the crate the plan chose (`cartalith-civ`: the lowest that builds
//! settlements and ways and still reaches `cartalith-engine`).
//!
//! # Where this follows the plan, and where it states a deviation
//!
//! * **Tiles.** The plan says "every tile" at every level up to `z_base + 6`.
//!   Level 10 alone is 4^10 = 1 048 576 tiles of 256^2 texels, so deep levels
//!   are measured as `K x K` **windows** of `W x W` contiguous tiles (defaults
//!   3x3 windows of 16x16 tiles, `W` capped at the level's own width, so
//!   levels with `2^z <= W` are measured **whole**). A window is also the
//!   unit `_nearest_tiles` actually orders -- the tiles one viewport wants --
//!   so (a) is scored on the question it answers today. Deviation, disclosed
//!   in the report.
//! * **Levels** run `z_base ..= z_base + 6` = 4..=10 at the shipped 256 px tile.
//!   The plan's "LOD entry level" is not a constant anywhere; `z_base` is the
//!   first level whose octave schedule is non-zero-capable, so it is the
//!   lowest level where "refinement adds nothing yet" can be observed
//!   directly (G_pt must be 0 there). Labelled judgement.
//! * **River gain** (`tile_rivers`, "not drawn") is NOT measured here: it
//!   needs a `carve_rivers = false` world (§5 EF-1: the carved world's `field`
//!   and `flow_discharge` are not self-consistent) and a `TilePlacement` per
//!   tile. It is reported as not run, never as 0.
//! * **Gain scalar.** The plan names the four gains but not the per-tile
//!   scalar the capture curve sums; this uses each gain's **RMS** (G_pt also
//!   keeps its max). Labelled judgement.
//!
//! Must never: edit generation or simulation code, or be read as a speed
//! (timings are explicitly outside EF-9.0).

